From e2fc1426219583d1dbc4ca8883e74ea0fb13c25c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:30:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] DEUNA/DELUA: BOOT port command; STOP, counters, load
 server, SET MAC fixes

The BOOT port command (known issue 109) puts the board into the primary
load state and asks a MOP load host for a secondary loader (Request
Program, program type 0; device type 1 DEUNA / 11 DELUA; to the load
server address or the load assistant multicast; repeated every 5 s, after
8 tries every 30 s with software ID 0).  The secondary loader runs on a
real board's own processor; SIMH does its work instead, as DEC's UNA
secondary loader does: Request Program for the tertiary loader (type 1),
Memory Loads into host memory answered by Request Memory Load, the load
host becomes the load server address, and the host, waiting in BR . at 2
with the CSR address at 4, is started with JMP @#transfer at 6/10 and
MOV #(4),R1 at 2.  SET XU DEBUG=BOOT logs the boot.

Found with DEC's tertiary loader TERUNA and fixed (DELUA User's Guide):
- STOP outside the running state and START in the running state are
  no-ops that set DNI, not port command errors (known issue 111);
- Read (and Clear) Counters writes only the UDB length in PCB+6, at most
  55 words (it always wrote 68 bytes; known issue 112);
- Read Load Server Address returned the multicast address exactly when a
  load server was set (known issue 113);
- SET XU MAC= also sets the current physical address, not only the one
  used after the next reset (known issue 114).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SuavtcpUxEC2vXhit3JaAg
