From 172e36b7d779f4816c7f30370d25498e1b6c1c2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:12:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] DEUNA/DELUA: BOOT XU command and HELP XU Booting topic
 (PDP-11)

BOOT XU (and BOOT XUB) puts a small bootstrap at 002000 that does what
DEC's M9312 'XE' boot ROM does: BR . at 2, the port's CSR address at 4,
the BOOT port command, JMP @#2.  The controller's boot engine then loads
the tertiary loader by MOP and starts it with R1 = CSR.  No ROM image is
needed; the 'XE' ROM route still works.  The VAX simulators keep no boot
routine.

HELP XU gets a "Booting" topic (PDP-11 only): BOOT XU, the ROM route as
the alternative, the MOP sequence, what the load host needs (VMS NCP
